Not quite the case.  Look in mcastu.c, specifically cast_wizard_spell():

    case MGC_CURSE_ITEMS:
        You_feel("as if you need some help.");
        rndcurse();
        dmg = 0;
        break;

case 9 for thrones in sit.c also has deterministic behaviour which can
be used to determine, without hitting 'i', whether you got your pack
cursed.  When you get the "A curse upon thee" message, you are struck
blind for rn1(100, 250) (I can never remember the order of the operands
to that one, and hate chasing down the definition, but I'm pretty sure
that that's either 100 to 349, or 250 to 349) turns if your Luck is
positive, but receive a dose of rndcurse() otherwise.

When Rodney harasses you from beyond the grave, you are always notified
of a black glow surrounding you (unless hallucinating, in which case
it's a random colour, or blind, in which case you can't see it) before
rndcurse() is called.

Of course, the most brutal item-cursing effect in the game is drinking
from a fountain and getting "This water's no good!".  Each item in your
inventory has a 20% chance of being hit with a cursing attempt,
regardless of magic resistance, HSPDAM, or even wielding Magicbane!
